  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Plaintext exists only at two decrypt points",
      "items": [
        "Decrypt point 1: the operator machine (git-crypt unlock / stdin); decrypt point 2: inside the Station process for HMAC.",
        "The env repo is ciphertext at rest, the network is inside SSH, and the image and logs contain no secret."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Root trust boundary (cannot be cryptographically removed)",
      "items": [
        "0600 + project namespacing block non-root users and other projects on the same host.",
        "But host root / the docker socket holder can read the plaintext env and container environ; model R1 assumes a trusted host.",
        "Hiding at-rest state from host root (R2) would require KMS/Vault fetch at boot, yet runtime memory stays visible — see runtime-secrets design §7.2."
      ]
    }
  ]
